@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy policy";
}

<section class="container py-5">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-lg-9">
            <div class="text-center mb-4" data-reveal>
                <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
                <h1 class="section-title mt-2">Privacy policy</h1>
                <p class="section-lead mx-auto mt-2">Last updated 16 November 2026</p>
            </div>

            <div class="glass p-4 p-lg-5" data-reveal="80">
                <h2 class="h5 mt-0">1. What we collect</h2>
                <p class="text-muted-silver">
                    We collect the name, contact number, email address, installation address and the identity
                    document that you supply when you place an order. For an employee of a retail partner we also
                    store the designation and the joining date. The service records - orders, connections, bills and
                    receipts - are created by the system as part of the normal business process.
                </p>

                <h2 class="h5">2. Uploaded documents</h2>
                <p class="text-muted-silver">
                    Identity proofs and supporting documents are uploaded in PDF, JPG or PNG format and must not be
                    larger than 2 MB. The files are stored outside the public web folder in a private storage area,
                    they receive a random file name and they are never served directly by the browser. A file can
                    only be opened through the system after the identity of the requester has been checked.
                </p>

                <h2 class="h5">3. How the data is used</h2>
                <p class="text-muted-silver">
                    The data serves to run the feasibility survey, to install the service, to prepare the invoices
                    and to keep the security deposit ledger. We never sell personal data and we do not pass it on
                    to third parties for marketing. Anonymous usage figures - the number of orders, connections
                    and cities - are shown on the public home page.
                </p>

                <h2 class="h5">4. Who can see your records</h2>
                <p class="text-muted-silver">
                    A customer sees only the orders, connections, bills and receipts that belong to the account. The
                    staff of a retail partner sees only the records of their own vendor. The administrator sees the
                    complete data set and is the only role that may approve vendors, plans and employees.
                </p>

                <h2 class="h5">5. Passwords and security</h2>
                <p class="text-muted-silver">
                    Passwords are stored as a salted hash, never in clear text. Five failed sign in attempts lock the
                    account for ten minutes. All forms carry an anti forgery token and every form that changes data
                    is written to an audit log with the name of the user, the time and the nature of the change.
                </p>

                <h2 class="h5">6. Retention and removal</h2>
                <p class="text-muted-silver">
                    Records are kept for the period required by the telecom regulations of the country. A customer
                    may ask for the deletion of the uploaded documents at any time; the operational records of a
                    billed service are kept as long as the account exists.
                </p>

                <h2 class="h5">7. Cookies</h2>
                <p class="text-muted-silver">
                    The website stores one cookie for the sign in token. No advertising or profiling cookie is used
                    anywhere on this system.
                </p>

                <h2 class="h5">8. Contact</h2>
                <p class="text-muted-silver">
                    Questions about the privacy policy are answered by the support desk at
                    <a href="mailto:support@nexus.com">support@nexus.com</a> or on 111-123456.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
